From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:22:09 -0400
Subject: folders: a nestable, collapsible tab container in the sidebar

FOLDER is a collection type in the tab tree (ADR 0013), deliberately not a
nested tab group: an outer group overwrites a tab's group id, so nesting
groups silently loses inner membership. A folder is created from a tab's
context menu, nests when the command is used on a tab already in a folder,
collapses from its header (hiding its tabs from Ctrl+Tab through the same
IsTabHidden contract as collapsed groups, nested included), and is renamed in
place by double-click. Dropping a dragged tab on a folder header appends it
to the folder and highlights the header while hovered; the header takes the
drop before the strip does through one hunk in TabDragController. Essentials
tabs never enter a folder.

Persistence: every tab carries its folder ancestry in per-tab session extra
data, rebuilt after restore through the same AddToNewFolder path. The
close-path use-after-free (a folder freed while it still owned its last tab)
is fixed and regression-tested; the drop handler that takes ownership of a
tab is tested with a fake controller, including a folder peeled out of the
tree mid-drag. The tab-strip mojom maps FOLDER to the plain container until
it grows a Folder variant.

docs/features/folders.md is the definition of done (F1-F11).

Folder paths are re-emitted through the session rebuild registry
(stedding_session_rebuild.h) so they survive the log being rebuilt from
scratch, and FolderPathForTab exposes the encoding the rebuild writes.

Why: folders were the highest Arc-named request on the comparable project;
users said they would not leave Arc without them, and folders without
drag-into are a gesture short.
Removable when: upstream ships an equivalent nestable, non-archiving tab
container with first-class collection persistence; ours then rebases onto it.
